`mz_b`: v2 improves over the physical prior but is worse than the v1 features-only baseline. This should be framed as unresolved yaw-moment modeling, not as a failed paper result. It is useful because it bounds the current deployable force-arm formulation and motivates yaw-specific feature/model work.([GitHub][2])

