## 5. Recommended Methods section structure

### 5.1 Classical aerodynamic prior

Explain the DeLaurier-like prior as the physical skeleton:

[
W_{\mathrm{prior}}(x)
=====================

\begin{bmatrix}
F_{\mathrm{prior}}(x) \
M_{\mathrm{prior}}(x)
\end{bmatrix}
]

where (x) includes wing phase/frequency, flight condition, airdata, body rates, and control-related quantities available to the simulator. Mention IsaacLab implementation and low-dimensional calibration only as prior construction, not as complete aerodynamic identification.([GitHub][6])

### 5.2 Effective wrench target

Define:

[
W_{\mathrm{eff}}(t)
===================

\begin{bmatrix}
F_{\mathrm{eff}}(t) \
M_{\mathrm{eff}}(t)
\end{bmatrix}
]

as the log-derived non-gravitational external wrench about the measured CG. State clearly that it includes the net effects required by the rigid-body equations and may include aerodynamic, mechanism, label, disturbance, and modeling effects.([GitHub][4])

### 5.3 Residual attribution

Define residuals:

[
R_F = F_{\mathrm{eff}} - F_{\mathrm{prior/corr}},
\quad
R_M = M_{\mathrm{eff}} - M_{\mathrm{prior/corr}}
]

Then describe correlation ranking, bins, held-out small-model ablations, and feature-group diagnostics. Use this only to motivate candidate features. The diagnostic file explicitly warns that this is not strict aerodynamic causal attribution.([GitHub][8])

### 5.4 Force correction

Recommended text structure:

[
F_{\mathrm{v2}}(x)
==================

F_{\mathrm{prior}}(x)
+
\Delta F_\theta(x,F_{\mathrm{prior}})
]

For selected v2:

* model form: affine correction;
* feature group: `base+rates+controls+lateral+interactions`;
* alpha = 1;
* selection metric: validation `force_mean` RMSE;
* test set used only after selection.

This is supported both by the result file and the training script’s force-candidate selection loop.([GitHub][2])

### 5.5 Force-arm moment correction

Recommended text structure:

[
M_{\mathrm{v2}}(x)
==================

\hat r_\phi(x) \times F_{\mathrm{v2}}(x)
+
\hat\tau_\psi(x)
]

where (\hat r_\phi(x)) is an effective force-arm correction and (\hat\tau_\psi(x)) is a free-torque residual term. This should be framed as an effective-wrench structure, not literal recovery of a physical instantaneous aerodynamic center.([GitHub][10])

### 5.6 Deployability constraints

State explicitly:

* no `true_force` input at inference;
* no target wrench or future information at inference;
* validation-only model selection;
* test set only for final reporting;
* diagnostic true-force dynamic-arm results are excluded from main deployable comparison;
* current result is log-prediction evidence, not closed-loop simulation validation.

These constraints are central to the paper’s credibility.([GitHub][2])

